WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:03.130
INTRO:
Near the end of last year, Rivian was the

00:00:03.130 --> 00:00:09.860
third most valuable automaker in the entire
world only beaten out by Toyota and Tesla.

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:14.830
This means that they had a higher valuation
than Volkswagen Daimler, General Motors, and

00:00:14.830 --> 00:00:15.910
Ford.

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:22.769
At the time, their market cap stood at an
eye watering $161 billion, and it’s not

00:00:22.769 --> 00:00:26.509
like they were delivering millions of vehicles
every single year.

00:00:26.509 --> 00:00:30.839
In fact, they had just started delivering
their first production vehicle the R1T.

00:00:30.839 --> 00:00:36.040
Since then, Rivian has produced and delivered
a few thousand vehicles throughout Q1, but

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:41.900
this is obviously not enough to justify a
$161 billion valuation either.

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:45.920
Fortunately though, the stock market has cooled
off quite a bit since the end of last year

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:48.320
which has annihilated Rivian stock.

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:53.960
In fact, their stock graph is literally just
a downward trend having sold off nearly 90%

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:54.960
from the peak.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:01:00.600
At the bottom, Rivian stood at a valuation
of $17.3 billion which is a far more reasonable

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:03.320
valuation for an up and coming EV startup.

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:08.490
But, Rivian is by no means out of the woods
yet, and it’ll likely take years for Rivian

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:10.670
to live up to their all time high valuation.

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:15.490
So, here’s the biggest issues plaguing Rivian
and why the stock remains risky despite it

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:18.920
having sold off 90%.

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:23.939
STARTUP:
Rivian has been around for quite some time

00:01:23.939 --> 00:01:26.170
having been founded in June of 2009.

00:01:26.170 --> 00:01:31.459
But, don’t kid yourself into thinking that
they’re mature company by any means.

00:01:31.459 --> 00:01:37.240
Developing, producing, and delivering vehicles
is an extremely long and tedious process,

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:41.900
so even though Rivian has been around for
13 years, they’re very much still just a

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:43.020
startup.

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:46.369
Not to mention, Rivian has taken it pretty
slow themselves.

00:01:46.369 --> 00:01:51.090
For example, Tesla was founded in 2003, and
they started delivering their first production

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:54.960
vehicle in 2008, so about 5 years later.

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:59.719
Meanwhile, it took Rivian 12 years to start
delivering their first production vehicle.

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:04.840
The brightside is that Rivian has been able
to perfect the R1T before launch, but from

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:09.030
an investor’s perspective, if it took them
12 years to deliver their first vehicle, how

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:13.320
long do you think it’ll take them to launch
cheaper vehicles and scale up production.

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:17.250
Historically, this wouldn’t have been that
big of a problem because it’s not like EV

00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:20.130
companies were facing that much competition
10 years ago.

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:26.330
But, today, legacy manufacturers such as Volkswagen,
Ford, and even GM have been taking EVs quite

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:27.330
seriously.

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:32.400
In fact, Bloomberg is predicting that Volkswagen
will overtake Tesla in EV sales by 2024 which

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:34.830
is only 18 months away.

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:39.280
They also think that GM and Ford will roughly
reach 1 million EV sales each by the end of

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:40.280
2025.

00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:45.140
So, Rivian is no longer the second biggest
EV company like they used to be.

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:50.310
Back in 2018, it used to be Tesla, Rivian,
and then some Chinese players, but that was

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:51.570
pretty much it.

00:02:51.570 --> 00:02:56.030
Now, legacy players are not only taking EVs
seriously, but they’re even catching up

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:57.190
to Tesla.

00:02:57.190 --> 00:03:00.930
Something else to note is that gas prices
are through the roof right now standing at

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:02.930
nearly $5 per gallon.

00:03:02.930 --> 00:03:08.230
This is no doubt terrible for everyday Americans,
but for upper middle class Americans who have

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:11.610
money, it makes more sense than ever to go
electric.

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:15.950
And that’s probably what they’ll do over
the next few years, but the problem is that

00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:18.320
Rivian isn’t here to capture all this new
demand.

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:20.740
I mean, what do you think is more likely.

00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:25.500
An American family buying an EV that’s already
on the market or an American family putting

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:29.570
in a pre order for a Rivian SUV that’ll
hopefully be delivered in 4 years.

00:03:29.570 --> 00:03:31.940
I think the answer is obvious.

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:36.720
Ideally, Rivian would’ve already had significant
scale like Tesla by the time that EV adoption

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:37.780
became more prominent.

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:42.110
But, it doesn’t look like Rivian is anywhere
close to this goal given that they produced

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:43.850
just 2500 EVs last quarter.

00:03:43.850 --> 00:03:48.610
To put that in perspective, Volkswagen produces
more cars in 2 hours.

00:03:48.610 --> 00:03:51.470
I’m not mentioning this to put down Rivian.

00:03:51.470 --> 00:03:55.140
Rather, I’m trying to show what they’re
going up against and why it’s going to be

00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:57.630
such an uphill battle for them moving forward.

00:03:57.630 --> 00:04:01.240
They really are just a startup that’s fighting
against dinosaurs.

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:05.550
This isn’t to say that Rivian can’t build
up their own niche customer base, but it does

00:04:05.550 --> 00:04:07.770
seem like Rivian missed out on the golden
period.

00:04:07.770 --> 00:04:13.380
A few years ago, if you wanted an EV, you
really only had one choice, buy a Tesla.

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:17.960
And I suspect that Rivian was hoping for a
similar position within the pickup market.

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:20.980
If you want an EV pickup, you have to go with
Rivian.

00:04:20.980 --> 00:04:26.410
This would’ve given them significant exposure
and demand, but the F-150 lightning is already

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:29.790
here which will likely stifle Rivian’s demand
significant.

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:34.780
And as more time goes by, it just becomes
more and more likely that the dinosaurs squash

00:04:34.780 --> 00:04:36.350
Rivian.

00:04:36.350 --> 00:04:41.170
SCALING UP:
Having to fight the legacy automakers head

00:04:41.170 --> 00:04:47.540
on is already bad enough, but Rivian has to
do that while also trying to scale up production.

00:04:47.540 --> 00:04:51.340
And based on Tesla’s experience with scaling
production, I think it’s safe to say that

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:54.320
scaling is by no means an easy feat.

00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:59.030
I mean, scaling model 3 production nearly
drove Tesla into bankruptcy.

00:04:59.030 --> 00:05:01.840
And Rivian is just now starting to scale up
production.

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:05.669
Rivian has some pretty ambitious targets when
it comes to scaling production.

00:05:05.669 --> 00:05:13.000
In February, they were hoping to get to 150,000
EVs per year by 2023, but honestly, this isn’t

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:14.030
that realistic.

00:05:14.030 --> 00:05:18.750
At their current rate of 2500 EVs per quarter,
we’re looking at annual production rate

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:20.910
of about 10,000 vehicles.

00:05:20.910 --> 00:05:24.560
Even if we give them the benefit of the doubt
and call it 20,000 vehicles, they’re basically

00:05:24.560 --> 00:05:26.820
where Tesla was at in 2013.

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:32.440
And it took Tesla 4 years to go from that
to Rivian’s goal of 150,000 EVs per year.

00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:37.380
So, realistically, it’ll probably take Rivian
till 2025 at the earliest to reach such numbers.

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:41.430
A bigger concern, however, is whether Rivian
will even have enough demand to produce so

00:05:41.430 --> 00:05:42.919
many vehicles.

00:05:42.919 --> 00:05:47.340
Right now, Rivian has 71,000 pre orders, and
this number will likely only grow as more

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:49.000
people start trusting the company.

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:54.290
But, these are the easiest orders to get because
all of these guys are EV enthusiasts who are

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:56.800
willing to wait years to get an EV pickup.

00:05:56.800 --> 00:06:00.180
As Rivian burns through these orders, however,
it’ll likely become a lot harder for them

00:06:00.180 --> 00:06:03.060
to garner sales given how expensive their
vehicles are.

00:06:03.060 --> 00:06:09.210
The R1T starts at $67,500 while the R1S starts
at $72,500.

00:06:09.210 --> 00:06:13.650
These prices make their vehicles completely
inaccessible to the vast majority of people.

00:06:13.650 --> 00:06:19.370
Now of course, Rivian has orders from Amazon,
but I don’t think serving Amazon is their

00:06:19.370 --> 00:06:20.740
long term goal.

00:06:20.740 --> 00:06:23.720
Their long term goal to become a premium EV
company.

00:06:23.720 --> 00:06:28.240
But, the only reason Tesla is able to sell
so many vehicles is thanks to their cheaper

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:35.470
Model 3 and Y. Throughout all of 2021, Tesla
only delivered roughly 25,000 Ss and Xs.

00:06:35.470 --> 00:06:39.949
This means that for it to make sense for Rivian
to scale to 150,000 vehicles per year, they

00:06:39.949 --> 00:06:44.250
would have to sell 6 times as many Model Ss
and Xs as Tesla sold last year.

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:49.010
I don’t think that’s an impossible goal
for Rivian, but that level of demand doesn’t

00:06:49.010 --> 00:06:50.780
just show up overnight.

00:06:50.780 --> 00:06:54.510
It takes years of deliveries, brand building,
and trust.

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:58.920
And to make things worse for Rivian, it looks
like we’re heading into a recession meaning

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:02.250
that it’s going to be significantly harder
to sell luxury vehicles.

00:07:02.250 --> 00:07:06.070
Even if we don’t enter a recession, it doesn’t
really matter because the fear of entering

00:07:06.070 --> 00:07:07.900
one has already set in.

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:13.340
And this will no doubt cause people to think
twice before buying a $70,000 pick up truck.

00:07:13.340 --> 00:07:17.250
Fortunately, Rivian can atleast slowly decrease
prices with time as their production process

00:07:17.250 --> 00:07:20.190
becomes more efficient which will hopefully
attract more customers.

00:07:20.190 --> 00:07:24.420
Wait, nevermind, they can’t do that either
due to insane inflation and the supply shortage

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:27.870
which have made raw materials and semiconductors
insanely expensive.

00:07:27.870 --> 00:07:33.139
They already increased their prices by $12,000
in March and this was likely just the first

00:07:33.139 --> 00:07:34.780
of many to come.

00:07:34.780 --> 00:07:38.480
Not only does this make it harder for Rivian
to sell their vehicles, but it also makes

00:07:38.480 --> 00:07:40.660
it harder for them scale production.

00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:45.270
Even companies as established as Apple are
dealing with supply constraints, so there’s

00:07:45.270 --> 00:07:50.040
no doubt that supply constraints will carry
over to Rivian as well.

00:07:50.040 --> 00:07:54.139
ABYSMAL FINANCIALS:
Aside from having to fight against the legacy

00:07:54.139 --> 00:07:59.320
players and deal with scaling production,
Rivian also has to deal with abysmal financials.

00:07:59.320 --> 00:08:04.320
Now, Rivian’s valuation has come down substantially,
and given how much cash they have, the intrinsic

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:07.850
value of the vehicles they’ve developed,
and their brand value, I don’t think they’re

00:08:07.850 --> 00:08:11.130
current valuation of $20 to $30 billion is
too crazy.

00:08:11.130 --> 00:08:16.050
I mean their total assets currently stand
at $21 billion, so they’re basically just

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:17.680
trading at book value.

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:22.639
So, their valuation isn’t that bad compared
to their assets and brand value, but their

00:08:22.639 --> 00:08:26.710
valuation is still ridiculous compared to
their revenue and net income figures.

00:08:26.710 --> 00:08:32.199
In the first quarter of 2022, Rivian only
pulled in $95 million worth of revenue, and

00:08:32.199 --> 00:08:37.880
to get this revenue, it cost them $597 million
meaning that their gross profit was negative

00:08:37.880 --> 00:08:39.520
half a billion dollars.

00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:42.990
Tack on half a billion dollars worth of R&amp;D
and another half a billion dollars worth of

00:08:42.990 --> 00:08:48.560
selling, general, and administrative expenses,
and your left with a net loss of $1.593 billion

00:08:48.560 --> 00:08:49.560
in a single quarter.

00:08:49.560 --> 00:08:53.580
At that rate, Rivian would burn through their
$16 billion cash reserves within a matter

00:08:53.580 --> 00:08:55.200
of 2.5 years.

00:08:55.200 --> 00:09:00.250
Fortunately, their financials should improve
with time, but I doubt they’ll become profitable

00:09:00.250 --> 00:09:04.110
anytime soon which means that they’ll have
to raise money sooner or later.

00:09:04.110 --> 00:09:08.630
And in the current stock market environment,
that’s not exactly an easy task.

00:09:08.630 --> 00:09:13.240
Rivian does have some notable backers including
Ford and Amazon, but they’re not exactly

00:09:13.240 --> 00:09:14.360
doing well themselves.

00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:19.101
In fact, Amazon lost money on their retail
business last quarter and their losses on

00:09:19.101 --> 00:09:21.730
Rivian just made their financial report look
even worse.

00:09:21.730 --> 00:09:24.960
To make things worse, Amazon stock itself
is down nearly 50%.

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:28.570
Meanwhile, Ford has been straight up cashing
out of their Rivian position.

00:09:28.570 --> 00:09:33.170
In May, Ford sold off tens of millions of
shares worth of Rivian which is not surprising

00:09:33.170 --> 00:09:36.020
given that they themselves are fighting for
survival.

00:09:36.020 --> 00:09:41.270
Last quarter, Ford lost $3.1 billion mostly
because of Rivian, and Ford can’t really

00:09:41.270 --> 00:09:46.360
afford this given that they already have $207
billion worth of liabilities.

00:09:46.360 --> 00:09:51.330
This isn’t to say that Amazon and Ford wouldn’t
bail out Rivian if they had to, but I don’t

00:09:51.330 --> 00:09:53.240
think they particularly want to.

00:09:53.240 --> 00:09:56.800
This means that most of the losses would have
to be paid for by public stock investors through

00:09:56.800 --> 00:09:57.800
share offerings.

00:09:57.800 --> 00:10:01.310
If you’re not familiar with what a share
offering is, it’s when a company issues

00:10:01.310 --> 00:10:04.760
new shares of their stock to raise money and
continue operations.

00:10:04.760 --> 00:10:08.600
Not only does this dilute existing shareholders,
but it adds significant amounts of selling

00:10:08.600 --> 00:10:10.440
pressure onto market.

00:10:10.440 --> 00:10:12.710
And there’s really no way around this.

00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:16.391
For Rivian to achieve the economies of scale
necessary to become profitable, they have

00:10:16.391 --> 00:10:20.160
to invest heavily into R&amp;D and factories and
scaling production.

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:25.210
So, Rivian is in for years of substantial
losses which just makes it even harder for

00:10:25.210 --> 00:10:27.690
the stock to gain any sort of bullish momentum.

00:10:27.690 --> 00:10:33.830
FUTURE OF RIVIAN:
Like many of my videos nowadays, this video

00:10:33.830 --> 00:10:35.640
hasn’t exactly been kind to Rivian.

00:10:35.640 --> 00:10:41.430
But, this isn’t to say that I don’t like
the company or that they’re gonna go bankrupt.

00:10:41.430 --> 00:10:46.740
Rivian’s R1T and R1S are phenomenal vehicles,
and it’s crazy to think that a startup was

00:10:46.740 --> 00:10:49.070
able to produce such high quality vehicles.

00:10:49.070 --> 00:10:52.890
In the future, when wait times cool down,
I would strongly consider Rivian when purchasing

00:10:52.890 --> 00:10:54.180
a vehicle for myself.

00:10:54.180 --> 00:10:59.500
But, while Rivian excites me as a customer,
it does not excite me as an investment.

00:10:59.500 --> 00:11:03.350
They have several years of hardship ahead
of them, and sky high inflation, the supply

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:07.250
shortage, and legacy players just make it
even harder for them to scale up and achieve

00:11:07.250 --> 00:11:08.340
profitability.

00:11:08.340 --> 00:11:11.990
And in a market where all stocks are getting
destroyed, there’s plenty of options when

00:11:11.990 --> 00:11:13.800
it comes to distressed stocks.

00:11:13.800 --> 00:11:18.850
And personally, Rivian just doesn't strike
me as the best of those options, but that’s

00:11:18.850 --> 00:11:20.070
just what I think.

00:11:20.070 --> 00:11:22.220
Would you guys rather by a Tesla or a Rivian?

00:11:22.220 --> 00:11:23.710
Comment that down below.

00:11:23.710 --> 00:11:28.560
Also, drop a like if you’re glad that bubble
valuations are finally coming back down to

00:11:28.560 --> 00:11:29.560
earth.

